    "en":  {
               "caution":  "Treat the November 23 surge cautiously: it was a sector-wide sympathy bounce, and QCOM still trades below its $169.14 Bollinger midline and $172–$174 EMA resistance cluster. Fundamentally, core smartphone silicon dropped 26% YoY, Apple\u0027s modem phase-out is ongoing, and QCT EBT margins are guided down to 20%–22% due to wafer/memory cost inflation and a 3-percentage-point data-center investment drag. If hyperscaler ramps slip or memory costs persist past H1 FY27, earnings pressure could linger.",
               "cons":  [
