                            "Foundry, packaging, and memory cost inflation will weigh on chip margins until pricing offsets land in H2 FY27.",
                            "Freedom Broker downgraded QCOM to Hold ($185) on November 9, while Baird ($300) and Susquehanna ($165) cut targets."
                        ],
               "fundamental":  "Qualcomm is navigating a sharp business mix shift. In Q4 FY26 (reported November 4, 2026), non-GAAP revenue fell 7.3% YoY to $10.44B and non-GAAP EPS dropped 28.3% to $2.17 as handset chips slumped 26% YoY ($5.14B) on memory tightness and Apple\u0027s modem exit. Yet diversification is accelerating: Automotive jumped 89% YoY to $1.99B, IoT rose 4% to $1.89B, and Q1 FY27 revenue is guided at $10.4B–$11.2B including $650M+ from Data Center custom silicon. On November 17, Qualcomm also expanded its Dragonfly AI200 inference rack into Cirrascale\u0027s cloud. Meanwhile, QTL licensing (~72%–76% EBT margin) is secured through 2030+ via Apple, Huawei, and Transsion renewals, keeping the patent moat intact while chip execution stays on watch.",
               "headline":  "Qualcomm Rebounds 10.3% in Chip Rally as Data Center AI Offsets Phone Slump",
