               "opportunity":  "For long-term AI-infrastructure holders, Qualcomm offers a rare combination of a locked-in high-margin patent base and fast-scaling new pillars. QTL renewals with Apple, Huawei, and Transsion protect cash flows through 2030+, funding a pivot where non-handset QCT sales are projected to grow over 60% YoY in FY27 and exceed half of chip revenue. If Qualcomm executes on its $5B FY27 data-center target (exiting at a $7B run-rate) alongside $8B-pace automotive growth, sentiment could re-rate sharply.",
               "opportunityCheck":  "Most sub-scores fit Qualcomm\u0027s current profile, but AI revenue exposure now looks too conservative and should move higher. On November 4, 2026, Qualcomm carved out Data Center as a formal QCT line, guiding at least $650M in Q1 FY27 and reiterating a $5B FY27 target backed by AWS custom silicon and Dragonfly AI200 inference. Conversely, bottleneck and pricing power should remain low: rising wafer, packaging, and memory costs are still squeezing chip margins through H1 FY27, showing limited near-term pricing leverage against hyperscalers and smartphone OEMs.",
